### 6. **Device & Peripheral Management (Add/Update)**

* **Page Title**: Device Management
* **Purpose**: Admins can add new devices or update status of existing ones
* **Description**: A form-driven management interface where admins can input device details and update inventory status. Supports profile-based classification and allows selective device availability. This helps streamline device onboarding and ensures new entries are standardized. It minimizes errors, simplifies deactivation of retired assets, and guarantees that users only see approved and available devices during request workflows.
* **Page Title**: Device Management
* **Purpose**: Admins can add new devices or update status of existing ones
* **Description**: A form-driven management interface where admins can input device details and update inventory status. Supports profile-based classification and allows selective device availability.
* **UI Components**:

  * **Form Section – Add New Device**:

    * Device Type: Dropdown (Laptop / Peripheral)
    * OS Type: Dropdown (Mac / Windows / Other)
    * Device Model: Dropdown (Pre-defined or free text)
    * User Profile Type: Dropdown (Executive / Standard / Performance)
    * Serial Number (optional)
    * Status Toggle (Available / Unavailable)
    * Submit Button
  * **Form Section – Update Existing**:

    * Select device by serial or device ID
    * Editable fields: Status, Assigned Profile
    * Save Changes Button
* **Interactions**:

  * Forms should have validation (e.g., required fields, dropdown dependencies)
  * Confirmation modals before saving changes
  * Show success or error toasts

